# Option B — Firebase onSnapshot Dashboard (Zero Polling)

## Goal
Replace the 15-second REST polling on `StudentLiveClassesPage.tsx` with Firebase Firestore
`onSnapshot` — so the student dashboard only fetches data when a class status **actually changes**.
No code changes to the class-join flow, attendance, Zoom integration, or any other module.

---

## How It Works (Big Picture)

```
TODAY (polling):
  Student browser → REST API → DB read  (every 15s × 1000 students = 1.2M reads/day)

AFTER OPTION B (event-driven):
  Backend cron detects status change
    → writes ONE tiny doc to Firestore: live_class_index/current
  All 1000 student browsers receive onSnapshot push instantly
    → each browser makes ONE REST call to refresh the list
  = ~2,000 reads total per status change event (vs 1.2M/day)
```

