## Proposed Changes

### Component 1 — Backend Signal Writer

#### [MODIFY] [liveSync.service.ts](file:///c:/Users/ASUS/OneDrive/Pictures/NERMAI_NEW/backend/services/liveSync.service.ts)

**Where:** Lines 82–111 — inside `syncClassStatus()`, right after `db.collection('classes').doc(cls.id).update(updatePayload)` on **line 95**.

**What:** After any class status change (UPCOMING→LIVE or LIVE→ENDED), write a single tiny
document to Firestore. This document acts as a "signal bell" — its sole job is to notify
all connected student browsers that something changed.

```typescript
// BEFORE (line 95):
await db.collection('classes').doc(cls.id).update(updatePayload);

// AFTER (add 7 lines after line 95):
await db.collection('classes').doc(cls.id).update(updatePayload);

// 🔔 Signal: notify all student dashboards of this status change via Firestore onSnapshot
await db.collection('live_class_index').doc('current').set({
  updatedAt: new Date().toISOString(),
  lastChangedClassId: cls.id,
  lastStatus: newStatus,
}, { merge: true });
```

**Why `merge: true`?** Prevents overwriting the document — it upserts only the changed fields.
This also means the first run creates the document automatically. No manual Firestore setup needed.

**Why `live_class_index/current`?** One single document for the entire LMS. All 1000 students
listen to this one document. When it changes, they all get notified simultaneously. The document
itself is tiny (~100 bytes) — it's not the actual class data, just a timestamp signal.

