## Firestore Security Rules

You must ensure students can **read** (not write) the `live_class_index` collection.
Add this to your Firestore rules:

```javascript
// In Firebase Console → Firestore → Rules
match /live_class_index/{docId} {
  allow read: if request.auth != null;   // any logged-in user can read
  allow write: if false;                 // only backend (Admin SDK) can write
}
```

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The backend uses the **Firebase Admin SDK** which bypasses rules entirely — it can always write.
> The rule `allow write: if false` only blocks client-side writes (browsers/apps), which is correct.

